# DB commands


# ✅ Step 1 — Connect to PostgreSQL (From VS Code Terminal)

Since you're using Docker:

docker exec -it persuade-db psql -U postgres -d persuade


You should now see:

persuade=#

# ✅ Step 2 — Check Main Wallet Balance

Your main wallet is is_main = true.

SELECT id, balance, is_main
FROM wallet
WHERE is_main = true;


This shows your vault balance.

# ✅ Step 3 — Check All User Wallets
SELECT id, user_id, balance
FROM wallet
WHERE is_main = false
ORDER BY user_id;

# ✅ Step 4 — Check Specific User Wallet

Example for user_id = 3:

SELECT id, user_id, balance
FROM wallet
WHERE user_id = 3;

# ✅ Step 5 — Clean View (Join Users + Wallet)

This is the best one for debugging:

SELECT u.id AS user_id,
       u.username,
       w.balance
FROM users u
JOIN wallet w ON u.id = w.user_id
WHERE w.is_main = false
ORDER BY u.id;

# ✅ Step 6 — See Total Vault Remaining
SELECT balance AS main_vault_balance
FROM wallet
WHERE is_main = true;

# ✅ Step 7 — See Recent Transactions
SELECT user_id,
       amount,
       decision,
       created_at
FROM transactions
ORDER BY created_at DESC
LIMIT 10;

# ✅ Step 8 — See Total Money Distributed
SELECT SUM(amount) AS total_distributed
FROM transactions
WHERE decision = 'APPROVED';

# ✅ Step 9 — Check Users Stats
SELECT id, username, wins, failed_attempts
FROM users
ORDER BY id;

# 🔥 Bonus Debug Command (Very Useful)

See vault + distributed side by side:

SELECT
    (SELECT balance FROM wallet WHERE is_main = true) AS main_balance,
    (SELECT SUM(amount) FROM transactions WHERE decision='APPROVED') AS total_paid;

# ✅ Exit psql
\q


# Reset Commands

Step 1 — Enter PostgreSQL
docker exec -it persuade-db psql -U postgres -d persuade

Step 2 — Reset All Data (Clean Reset)

Run this:

TRUNCATE TABLE transactions RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;
TRUNCATE TABLE sessions RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;
TRUNCATE TABLE wallet RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;
TRUNCATE TABLE users RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;
TRUNCATE TABLE global_stats RESTART IDENTITY CASCADE;


This will:

Delete all rows

Reset auto-increment IDs

Keep table structure

Step 3 — Recreate Main Wallet

After truncating, you must recreate your main vault:

INSERT INTO wallet (balance, is_main)
VALUES (30000, true);

Step 4 — Recreate Global Stats
INSERT INTO global_stats (total_wins, security_level)
VALUES (0, 1);

Step 5 — Verify Reset

Check:

SELECT * FROM wallet;
SELECT * FROM users;
SELECT * FROM transactions;
SELECT * FROM global_stats;


You should see:

Only 1 wallet (main)

Empty users

Empty transactions

Global stats reset


# Reinsert users

✅ Step 1 — Enter PostgreSQL
docker exec -it persuade-db psql -U postgres -d persuade

✅ Step 2 — Insert 30 Users

This will generate users user_1 to user_30.

INSERT INTO users (username, failed_attempts, wins, last_attempt_time)
SELECT 
    'user_' || generate_series(1,30),
    0,
    0,
    NOW();

✅ Step 3 — Create Wallet For Each User

Each user gets balance = 0.

INSERT INTO wallet (user_id, balance, is_main)
SELECT id, 0, false
FROM users;

✅ Step 4 — Verify Users
SELECT id, username FROM users ORDER BY id;


You should see 30 rows.

✅ Step 5 — Verify Wallets
SELECT user_id, balance
FROM wallet
WHERE is_main = false
ORDER BY user_id;


You should see 30 user wallets.

✅ Step 6 — Confirm Main Wallet Still Exists
SELECT id, balance
FROM wallet
WHERE is_main = true;


You should still have your vault with 30000.

🔥 Bonus: Check Everything Together
SELECT u.id, u.username, w.balance
FROM users u
JOIN wallet w ON u.id = w.user_id
ORDER BY u.id;